  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "NT L-mode confinement enhancement (H_98 = 1.44) scales favorably to burning-plasma conditions, validating extrapolation from TCV/DIII-D non-burning experiments",
      "Ohmic-only operation is feasible at compact high-field NT conditions (H_NA ≥ 2), enabling Q ≈ 500 with zero auxiliary heating per Ball et al. 2024",
      "NT geometry passively delivers low scrape-off-layer power (P_SOL = 23.5 MW, only 5.2% of fusion power) enabling conventional tungsten monoblock divertor",
      "REBCO HTS TF coils at 11 T with demountable joints and 40% margin to critical current survive cumulative 14 MeV neutron + gamma irradiation at fusion fluence",
      "FLiBe liquid immersion blanket simultaneously serves as breeder, coolant, and shield achieving TBR = 1.15 with self-healing molybdenum barrier",
      "Passive stabilizer plates (inboard and outboard, uniquely enabled by NT X-point geometry) resolve NT's intrinsic vertical instability at reactor-relevant elongation and poloidal beta",
      "Net electric output scales from MANTA's 90 MWe pilot to commercial 1 GW+ class while maintaining NT-specific cost advantages"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Advanced divertor engineering — Super-X, snowflake, and liquid metal divertor concepts unnecessary because NT's low P_SOL keeps peak heat flux (2.8 MW/m²) within demonstrated tungsten monoblock limits",
      "Auxiliary heating capital cost — ~$150M for 40 MW ICRF system entirely eliminated if ohmic-only scenario (H_NA ≥ 2) is validated (~4% of overnight cost)",
      "Active impurity seeding and high-radiated-power-fraction (90–95%) control systems that PT designs require to reach comparable heat flux numbers",
      "Specialized perpendicular-plate divertor geometry and complex plasma control hardware needed for fully detached PT operation",
      "ELM mitigation systems (RMP coils, pellet pacing) — NT operates ELM-free in L-mode, removing a class of PT engineering line items"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "NT passive vertical stabilizer plates (~$15–60M, central estimate $30M) — NT-specific infrastructure absent from MANTA cost accounting and from PT tokamak cost analogues",
      "FLiBe-to-molten-salt (NaNO₃/KNO₃) heat exchanger at fusion-plant scale — explicitly flagged 'low TRL' in MANTA, no commercial supply chain",
      "Thermal energy storage buffer sized for the 15-min pulse / 2-min dwell quasi-steady operation cycle, absent from steady-state designs",
      "V-4Cr-4Ti vacuum vessel (~1 cm thick) — nuclear-grade alloy with no industrial supply chain at multi-hundred-tonne scale",
      "NT-specific TF coil geometry with demountable joints — coil shape constraints not faced by conventional tokamaks, increasing coil engineering complexity beyond standard REBCO TF designs"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "NT confinement scaling to burning-plasma conditions is unvalidated — entire economic case rests on H_98 and H_NA factors extrapolated from non-burning L-mode TCV/DIII-D experiments; if confinement advantage does not persist at high alpha-particle pressure and impurity concentrations, cost-reduction claims collapse",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Net electric output is far below commercial viability — MANTA produces only 90 MWe net from 450 MW fusion (Q_e = 2.4) with LCOE $396/MWh (~3× offshore wind, ~6× ARIES-ACT $64/MWh target); no credible path from Firefly's 50–100 MW design point to commercial LCOE without major upscaling",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Ohmic-only hypothesis (Q ≈ 500) depends on H_NA = 2 confinement enhancement based on preliminary 0D power balance and TCV data — if H_NA ≈ 1, ohmic heating insufficient and full $100–500M auxiliary heating system required",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "TF coil cost ($1.5B of $3.4B, ~44%) is dominant cost driver and unaffected by NT geometry — NT savings only address secondary cost categories, leaving a hard magnet-cost floor that NT cannot overcome",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Commercial-scale NT plant cost study does not exist — MANTA is a sub-commercial pilot, no 1 GW+ NT tokamak design has been published, leaving extrapolation to commercial plant cost essentially unanchored",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Firefly Fusion has disclosed no proprietary plasma parameters, blanket design, tritium cycle approach, or power conversion cycle — all Firefly-specific values are aspirational press statements",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "FLiBe-to-molten-salt heat exchanger explicitly flagged 'low TRL' in MANTA — fusion-scale technology does not exist; tritium permeation through HX surfaces is unresolved",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "V-4Cr-4Ti vacuum vessel has no commercial production at the multi-hundred-tonne scale required; no industrial supply chain for nuclear-grade material with controlled impurities",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO tape supply chain bottleneck — global production at thousands km/year vs. 5,000+ km needed per plant; commercial price target ~$10/kA-m vs. current $30–100/kA-m",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "FLiBe supply chain constrained by beryllium (~300 t/year global, Materion-dominated) and Li-6 enrichment (Russian/Chinese mercury amalgam capacity)",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "NT vertical stability is intrinsically worse than PT and degrades at higher poloidal beta — passive stabilizer plate infrastructure absent from MANTA cost accounting; reactor-scale validation gap remains",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium fuel cycle TRL 3–4 — kg/day-scale closed-loop breeding from FLiBe never demonstrated; MANTA acknowledges 'a fully functioning tritium fuel cycle has yet to be developed or tested'",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Capacity factor uncertainty — MANTA pilot at 37%, model assumes 80% commercial; LCOE elasticity to availability is -0.97 (largest engineering sensitivity)",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "PF2 coil lifetime (~890 MW·yr ≈ 2 full-power-years) sets demanding maintenance cycle requiring radiation-hardened remote handling not yet demonstrated at scale",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium global inventory ~25–30 kg declining at 5.5%/year from CANDU byproduction — startup inventory ~440g per plant creates fleet-deployment sequencing constraint shared with all D-T concepts",
        "severity": "low"
      }
